      "action": "execute_python",
      "action_input": {
        "code": "import csv\n\ntotal_weight = 0\ncount = 0\n\nwith open('csv/superhero.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        if row['gender_id'] == '2':\n            weight = row['weight_kg']\n            if weight and weight != '':\n                total_weight += float(weight)\n                count += 1\n\nif count > 0:\n    avg_weight = total_weight / count\n    print(f\"Average weight of female superheroes: {avg_weight}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No female superheroes found\")"
      },
      "raw_response": "```json\n{\"thought\":\"I now understand the data structure. Gender_id 2 corresponds to Female. I need to calculate the average weight_kg for all rows where gender_id = 2.\",\"action\":\"execute_python\",\"action_input\":{\"code\":\"import csv\\n\\ntotal_weight = 0\\ncount = 0\\n\\nwith open('csv/superhero.csv', 'r') as f:\\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\\n    for row in reader:\\n        if row['gender_id'] == '2':\\n            weight = row['weight_kg']\\n            if weight and weight != '':\\n                total_weight += float(weight)\\n                count += 1\\n\\nif count > 0:\\n    avg_weight = total_weight / count\\n    print(f\\\"Average weight of female superheroes: {avg_weight}\\\")\\nelse:\\n    print(\\\"No female superheroes found\\\")\"}}\n```",
